1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
湖南人吃鱼，专挑最肥的鱼头
In Hunan, the fattest part is the head

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,400
一劈两半，根部不断
Split in two, still joined at the base

3
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:06,600
盐、料酒先腌一腌
Salted, splashed with rice wine

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,800
铺满一勺红剁椒
Buried under a spoon of red chili

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,000
豆豉、蒜末，一起上锅蒸
Black beans, garlic — then straight to steam

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
辣味钻进每一丝鱼肉
The heat seeps into every flake

7
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,600
相传源自一位逃难的文人
Legend traces it to a fugitive scholar

8
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,800
农家用自种辣椒蒸河鱼
A farm wife steamed river fish in homegrown chili

9
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:20,000
2024年，列入湖南省级非遗
In 2024, named provincial heritage

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,200
撒把葱花，红配绿，真"韵味"
Scallions on top — Hunan calls it "yùnwèi"

11
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,400
最下饭的，是蒸出的那勺汤
Best part? The chili broth over rice

12
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,000
你能吃多辣？下集·水煮鱼
How hot can you go? Next: boiled fish
